  "Scenes.Lumberjack.DrinkQuestion": "Grinning, the woodsman elaborates, [say: It's a recipe going far back in my family.] He pulls up a sack of wood chips. [say: I soak particular choice types of wood for about two or three days in a cloth bag. At this point, I wring it all out. A few spices, like cinnamon or whatever I can easily get my hands on, and healthy amounts of bourbon go into a pot to heat with the rest of the drink.] "
